// ============================================================
// v10.155 FIX 12 - S12b REMOVED
//
// S12b shuffled a single series and asked whether the observed AC1 was
// higher than a random reordering would give. That null hypothesis is
// "this series is white noise" - which EVERY real sea-surface-temperature
// pixel rejects, for ordinary physical reasons that have nothing to do
// with resilience. The module's own shipping validation recorded the
// problem without naming it: "structured data -> p=0.0000". Seasonal data
// is structured. So is every ocean pixel. A test that fires everywhere
// carries no information.
//
// The correct null preserves the power spectrum (phase randomisation or
// IAAFT). But lag-1 autocorrelation is essentially DETERMINED by the power
// spectrum, so a spectrum-preserving surrogate makes an AC1 test
// near-vacuous by construction. There is no version of this module that
// answers a useful question about AC1, which is why it is deleted rather
// than repaired.
//
// What replaces it: nothing is lost. S13's COMPARE tests whether two
// windows are EXCHANGEABLE, which is a different and answerable question,
// and its permutation test was measured at a 0-9% false-positive rate on
// 13.6 years of no-event Scripps Pier CTD data.
//
// permutationTestAC1Fixed() is left defined above but is now unreferenced.
// ============================================================

